;; cljfmt does not know that `prop/for-all` binds names and then takes a body,
;; so by default it indents the property under the binding vector as though the
;; body were a second argument. Saying so here keeps a generative test looking
;; like the `let` it reads as.
;;
;; `:extra-indents`, not `:indents`: the latter replaces cljfmt's default rules
;; outright, which silently unsets the ones for `defn`, `let` and `ns` and
;; reformats the whole project.
{:extra-indents {clojure.test.check.properties/for-all [[:block 1]]
                 prop/for-all                          [[:block 1]]}}
